(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_zoology_humanhealthanddisease=[{id:"neet-2026r-q151",pn:151,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Lymphoid organs",q:`Which of the following are secondary lymphoid organs?
(a) Bone marrow
(b) Tonsils
(c) Spleen
(d) Thymus
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["(b) and (c) only","(b) and (d) only","(a) and (d) only","(a) and (b) only"],c:0,s:`Bone marrow and thymus are primary lymphoid organs.
Tonsils and spleen are secondary lymphoid organs.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q155",pn:155,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Sexually transmitted diseases",q:"Which of the following disease is not sexually transmitted?",o:["Tuberculosis","Gonorrhoea","Genital warts","Syphilis"],c:0,s:`Genital warts, syphilis and gonorrhoea are sexually transmitted diseases.
Genital warts are caused by Human papilloma virus.
Syphilis is caused by Treponema pallidum.
Gonorrhoea is caused by Neisseria gonorrhoeae.
Tuberculosis is caused by Mycobacterium tuberculosis and spreads through air.`},{id:"neet-2026-q157",pn:157,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Drugs and their effects",q:`Match List I with List II:
List I (Drug) \u2014 List II (Effect)
A. Nicotine \u2014 I. Causes sense of euphoria and increased energy
B. Morphine \u2014 II. Stimulates adrenal gland to release catecholamines into blood circulation
C. Heroin \u2014 III. Effective sedative and painkiller
D. Cocaine \u2014 IV. A depressant; slows down body function`,o:["A-III, B-II, C-IV, D-I","A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I","A-II, B-III, C-I, D-IV","A-III, B-II, C-I, D-IV"],c:1,s:`Nicotine is present in tobacco. It stimulates the adrenal medulla to release catecholamines into blood, so A \u2192 II.
Morphine is an opioid and an effective sedative and painkiller, so B \u2192 III.
Heroin is a depressant and slows down body function, so C \u2192 IV.
Cocaine is a stimulant and gives a sense of euphoria and increased energy, so D \u2192 I.
Thus A \u2192 II, B \u2192 III, C \u2192 IV, D \u2192 I.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q164",pn:164,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Malaria, Plasmodium life cycle",q:"Which of the following statements is correct about Plasmodium?",o:["Reproduces sexually in RBCs","Gametocytes develop in mosquito gut","Fertilization takes place in mosquito gut","Reproduces sexually in liver cells"],c:2,s:`Plasmodium reproduces asexually in liver cells.
It also reproduces asexually in red blood cells, which burst and cause cycles of fever. Released parasites infect new RBCs.
A female Anopheles mosquito takes up gametocytes with its blood meal.
Fertilization and development take place in the mosquito's gut.
The sexual stages (gametocytes) develop in RBCs.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q167",pn:167,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Immunity and antibodies",q:"Colostrum, secreted by mother during initial days of lactation, is abundant in ________.",o:["IgM","IgA","IgD","IgG"],c:1,s:`Colostrum, secreted by the mother in the initial days of lactation, is abundant in IgA antibody.
IgG antibody passes through the placenta and gives natural passive immunity.`},{id:"neet-2026-q170",pn:170,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Plasmodium life cycle",q:`The following are the stages of life cycle of Plasmodium. Arrange the stages in the proper order.
A. The parasites reproduce asexually in RBCs, bursting the cells.
B. The parasites reproduce asexually in liver cells, bursting the cells and releasing into blood.
C. Gametocytes develop in RBCs.
D. Sporozoites reach the liver through the blood.
E. Female mosquito injects sporozoites into humans during bite.
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["A, B, C, D, E","E, D, B, A, C","C, A, B, D, E","E, C, D, B, A"],c:1,s:`Plasmodium enters the human body as sporozoites through the bite of an infected female Anopheles mosquito (E).
The sporozoites reach the liver through the blood (D).
The parasites first multiply asexually in liver cells, which burst and release them into the blood (B).
They then attack the RBCs and multiply asexually, causing rupture of the cells (A).
Sexual stages (gametocytes) develop in red blood cells (C).
When a female Anopheles bites an infected person, these parasites enter the mosquito's body and develop further.
Order: E, D, B, A, C.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q172",pn:172,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Drugs and abuse",q:"Which of the following is used as an effective sedative and painkiller for treating post-surgery patients?",o:["Antibiotics","Morphine","Anti-retroviral drugs","Interferon"],c:1,s:`Morphine is a very effective sedative and painkiller, useful for patients who have had surgery.
Interferon belongs to the cytokine barrier of innate immunity.
Antibiotics are used to stop the growth of bacteria.`},{id:"neet-2025-q120",pn:120,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Cancer",q:`Which are correct:
A. Computed tomography and magnetic resonance imaging detect cancers of internal organs.
B. Chemotherapeutics drugs are used to kill non-cancerous cells.
C. \u03B1-interferon activate the cancer patients' immune system and helps in destroying the tumour.
D. Chemotherapeutic drugs are biological response modifiers.
E. In the case of leukaemia blood cell counts are decreased.
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["B and D only","D and E only","C and D only","A and C only"],c:3,s:`Statements A and C are correct.
Statements B, D and E are incorrect.
Chemotherapeutic drugs are used to kill cancerous cells.
In case of leukaemia, blood cell counts are increased.
\u03B1-interferons are biological response modifiers.`},{id:"neet-2025-q135",pn:135,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Cancer",q:`Neoplastic characteristics of cells refer to :
A. A mass of proliferating cell
B. Rapid growth of cells
C. Invasion and damage to the surrounding tissue
D. Those confined to original location
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["A, B only","A, B, C only","A, B, D only","B, C, D only"],c:1,s:`The correct answer is A, B and C only.
A neoplasm is a general term for any abnormal growth of tissue.
Neoplastic characteristics: a mass of proliferating cells, rapid growth, invasion and damage to surrounding tissue.
Cancer refers to malignant neoplasms, which are cancerous and invasive.
Benign tumours stay confined to their original location, so D is not included.
Malignant tumours are a mass of proliferating (neoplastic or tumour) cells that grow very rapidly, invading and damaging surrounding normal tissues.`},{id:"neet-2025-q143",pn:143,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Antibody structure",q:"Identify the statement that is NOT correct.",o:["Each antibody has two light and two heavy chains.","The heavy and light chains are held together by disulfide bonds.","Antigen binding site is located at C-terminal region of antibody molecules.","Constant region of heavy and light chains are located at C-terminus of antibody molecules"],c:2,s:`Each antibody molecule has four peptide chains: two small light chains and two longer heavy chains.
So an antibody is written as H\u2082L\u2082.
In an antibody molecule the antigen binding site is at the N-terminal region, not the C-terminal region.`},{id:"neet-2025-q156",pn:156,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Lymphoid organs",q:`After maturation, in primary lymphoid organs, the lymphocytes migrate for interaction with antigens to secondary lymphoid organ(s) / tissue(s) like
A. thymus
B. bone marrow
C. spleen
D. lymph nodes
E. Peyer\u2019s patches
Choose the correct answer from the options given below`,o:["B, C, D only","A, B, C only","E, A, B only","C, D, E only"],c:3,s:`The primary lymphoid organs are bone marrow and thymus, where immature lymphocytes become antigen-sensitive lymphocytes.
After maturation they migrate to secondary lymphoid organs like spleen, lymph nodes, Peyer\u2019s patches of the small intestine and appendix.
These secondary organs are the sites where lymphocytes interact with the antigen.`},{id:"neet-2025-q167",pn:167,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Immunity types",q:"Which of the following type of immunity is present at the time of birth and is a non-specific type of defence in the human body?",o:["Acquired Immunity","Innate Immunity","Cell-mediated Immunity","Humoral Immunity"],c:1,s:`Innate immunity is a non-specific defence present at birth. It works by barriers that stop foreign agents entering the body.
Acquired immunity is pathogen specific and has memory cells.
The response by B-lymphocytes is humoral immunity.
The response by T-lymphocytes is cell-mediated immunity.`},{id:"neet-2024-q151",pn:151,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Diseases and causative agents",q:`Match List I with List II :
A. Typhoid \u2014 I. Fungus
B. Leishmaniasis \u2014 II. Nematode
C. Ringworm \u2014 III. Protozoa
D. Filariasis \u2014 IV. Bacteria
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II","A-II, B-IV, C-III, D-I","A-I, B-III, C-II, D-IV","A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II"],c:3,s:`Typhoid is caused by Salmonella typhimurium (bacteria).
Leishmaniasis is caused by the protozoan Leishmania donovani.
Ringworm is caused by fungi of the genera Microsporum, Trichophyton and Epidermophyton.
Filariasis is caused by Wuchereria bancrofti and Wuchereria malayi (nematodes).
So A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II.`},{id:"neet-2024-q160",pn:160,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Autoimmune disorders",q:`Which of the following are Autoimmune disorders?
A. Myasthenia gravis
B. Rheumatoid arthritis
C. Gout
D. Muscular dystrophy
E. Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE)
Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :`,o:["B, C & E only","C, D & E only","A, B & D only","A, B & E only"],c:3,s:`Myasthenia gravis, rheumatoid arthritis and SLE are autoimmune disorders.
Muscular dystrophy is a genetic disorder that slowly affects skeletal muscles.
Gout is joint inflammation from uric acid crystals.
So only A, B and E are autoimmune.`},{id:"neet-2024-q171",pn:171,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Drugs and their sources",q:`Match List I with List II:
A. Cocaine \u2014 I. Effective sedative in surgery
B. Heroin \u2014 II. Cannabis sativa
C. Morphine \u2014 III. Erythroxylum
D. Marijuana \u2014 IV. Papaver somniferum`,o:["A-II, B-I, C-III, D-IV","A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II","A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II","A-I, B-III, C-II, D-IV"],c:1,s:`Option (2) is correct.
A. Cocaine comes from Erythroxylum coca and stimulates the CNS.
B. Heroin is made by acetylation of morphine, which comes from Papaver somniferum.
C. Morphine comes from Papaver somniferum and is an effective sedative in surgery.
D. Marijuana comes from Cannabis sativa; it is hallucinogenic and affects the cardiovascular system.`},{id:"neet-2024-q180",pn:180,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Diseases and pathogens",q:`Match List I with List II :
A. Common cold \u2014 I. Plasmodium
B. Haemozoin \u2014 II. Typhoid
C. Widal test \u2014 III. Rhinoviruses
D. Allergy \u2014 IV. Dust mites`,o:["A-III, B-I, C-II, D-IV","A-IV, B-II, C-III, D-I","A-II, B-IV, C-III, D-I","A-I, B-III, C-II, D-IV"],c:0,s:`Common cold is caused by rhinoviruses.
Haemozoin is released into the blood when RBCs rupture after Plasmodium infection.
Widal test is used to confirm typhoid fever.
Allergy can be caused by dust mites.
So A-III, B-I, C-II, D-IV.`},{id:"neet-2024-q193",pn:193,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Lymphoid organs",q:`Given below are two statements :
Statement I : Bone marrow is the main lymphoid organ where all blood cells including lymphocytes are produced.
Statement II : Both bone marrow and thymus provide micro environments for the development and maturation of T-lymphocytes.
In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :`,o:["Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.","Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct.","Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.","Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect."],c:2,s:`Both statements are correct.
In humans the bone marrow is the main lymphoid organ where all blood cells, including lymphocytes, are produced.
Bone marrow and thymus both give the micro-environment for development and maturation of T-lymphocytes.
Options (1), (2) and (4) are wrong.`},{id:"neet-2023-q158",pn:158,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Common diseases and pathogens",q:`Match List I with List II.
List I: A. Ringworm; B. Filariasis; C. Malaria; D. Pneumonia
List II: I. Haemophilus influenzae; II. Trichophyton; III. Wuchereria bancrofti; IV. Plasmodium vivax
Choose the correct answer from the options given below :`,o:["A-III, B-II, C-IV, D-I","A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I","A-II, B-III, C-I, D-IV","A-III, B-II, C-I, D-IV"],c:1,s:`Ringworm is caused by Trichophyton.
Filariasis is caused by Wuchereria bancrofti.
Malaria is caused by Plasmodium species.
Pneumonia is caused by Haemophilus influenzae.`},{id:"neet-2023-q161",pn:161,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"Drugs and their effects",q:`Match List I with List II :
List I: A. Heroin; B. Marijuana; C. Cocaine; D. Morphine
List II: I. Effect on cardiovascular system; II. Slow down body function; III. Painkiller; IV. Interfere with transport of dopamine.
Choose the correct answer from the options given below :`,o:["A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II","A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III","A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV","A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I"],c:1,s:`Heroin is an opioid depressant that slows body functions (A-II).
Marijuana affects the cardiovascular system (B-I).
Cocaine interferes with transport of the neurotransmitter dopamine (C-IV).
Morphine is a sedative and painkiller (D-III).`},{id:"neet-2023-q166",pn:166,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Human Health and Disease",st:"AIDS and HIV",q:"In which blood corpuscles, the HIV undergoes replication and produces progeny viruses?",o:["Eosinophils","TH cells","B-lymphocytes","Basophils"],c:1,s:`HIV enters helper T-lymphocytes (TH cells) and replicates there.
The new viruses released into blood attack more helper T cells.`}]})();
